================================================================================ 2. PERMITTED USES (INTERNAL COLLABORATORS)
================================================================================

The following uses are permitted ONLY for individuals who have been
expressly authorized in writing by UNSCH, acting through the OTI, in
their capacity as:

a) Employees or contractors of UNSCH assigned to the OTI;
b) Members of an internal development team with an active contribution
agreement;
c) Students performing supervised academic practice (pre-profesional
or profesional internships) under an active agreement with UNSCH;
d) Public officials of cooperating Peruvian government entities
explicitly designated by OTI for a documented collaboration.

For these authorized collaborators, the following is permitted,
strictly within the scope of the documented collaboration and subject
to the restrictions of Section 3:

- Reading and downloading the source code for the purpose of
  contributing back to the project;
- Forking the repository for the purpose of submitting proposed
  changes via Pull Request;
- Reproducing, in executable form, the Software in development,
  staging, or production environments operated by or for UNSCH.

